/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/opus/5/002/codegen_logs/8.full.log:6109:1279457       00:57  0.0  0.0 node /home/lixinyu/.nvm/versions/node/v18.20.8/bin/codex exec --skip-git-repo-check -c model="gpt-5.4" -c reasoning.effort="high" 请严格执行下面的 ARC 新题代码生成提示词。必须把代码写入 prompt 指定的目标路径，并运行 prompt 里的自检命令。生成代码前必须把 `/home/lixinyu/snap/new/solvers/arc_utils.py` 作为公共参考工具箱快速阅读，优先复用其中的坐标、bbox、连通域、裁剪、变换和颜色等通用实现；若直接 import，必须保证目标文件可被 `SourceFileLoader` 直接加载。  执行每个代码生成 prompt 时，还必须遵守以下语义一致性硬约束：  1. 输出必须唯一可判定    输入中的线索必须足以唯一确定目标对象、目标操作和结果。    不允许依赖含糊解释，或让同一可见线索在不同语境下产生不同答案。    注意不可多个不同样例的输入网格处理后的输出网格都相同  2. 组合步骤必须不可替代    题目描述中的关键步骤都应对结果产生必要影响。    不能让某一步只是表面存在，实际可被更简单的捷径完全替代。  3. 实现必须遵守题面定义的参照系    所有判断、匹配、距离、对称、排序、分区等，都必须使用题面指定的对象范围和坐标参照。    不得为了实现方便换成另一套参照系。  4. 生成样例要覆盖反例    生成器要主动产生能排除错误捷径的样例。    不只生成最容易通过的标准形态，还要覆盖边界情况、分支情况和易混淆情况。  5. 验证要检查语义而不只是自洽    不能只验证 main(generate_input()) 能闭环。    还要检查实现是否真的满足题面规则、关键依赖、唯一性和非退化性。  你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。  ## 新题位置  - 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/des/opus/5` - 题号：`8` - 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/key_combo/code/opus/5/012/8.py`  ## 新题描述  <new_puzzle index="8"> ## 新题 8：墙壁滑动后像素数决定正方形重排  **组合逻辑**：[滑动(slide) + 同色物体朝同色墙(same_color_wall) + 碰撞停止(collision_stop)] → 像素聚合计数(创新：同色物体滑动到墙壁后合并计数) → [压缩重排(repack) + 像素数定边长(pixel_count_determines_side) + 面积递增排列(area_ascending_order)]  **来源原语**：滑动、墙壁列、同色物体朝同色墙、近者优先不重叠、碰撞停止（f0100645）；压缩重排、像素数定边长、面积递增排列、排序（8abad3cf）  **依赖链**：同色物体滑动到各自的墙壁列 → 滑动后同色物体可能在墙壁旁合并为更大的连通区域 → 合并后每种颜色的总像素数决定其正方形边长 → 所有颜色的正方形按面积递增排列输出。滑动改变了物体之间的邻接关系，直接影响像素计数；计数决定正方形尺寸。  将不同颜色的散布物体分别滑向同色墙壁列，滑动后每种颜色的总像素数开方得到正方形边长，按面积从小到大排列输出。  **输入结构**：约 12x12 的网格。背景为黑(0)。最左列全部为红(2)，最右列全部为蓝(1)，形成两面彩色墙壁。网格中间区域散布若干红(2) 和蓝(1) 的 8-连通物体（每个 2~5 像素，形状不规则），以及若干绿(3) 物体。绿(3) 不对应任何墙壁。生成约束：红(2) 物体的总像素数（不含墙壁列）和蓝(1) 物体的总像素数（不含墙壁列）各自为完全平方数（如 4、9、16）；绿(3) 的总像素数也为完全平方数。各物体之间互不相邻。  **规则**： 1. 红(2) 物体向左滑向红(2) 墙壁列：按距左墙壁的距离从近到远依次处理。每个物体整体水平左移，直到物体的最左像素紧邻墙壁列或紧邻已停靠的红色物体的右边缘。清除物体原位置。 2. 蓝(1) 物体向右滑向蓝(1) 墙壁列：按距右墙壁的距离从近到远依次处理。每个物体整体水平右移，直到物体的最右像素紧邻墙壁列或紧邻已停靠的蓝色物体的左边缘。清除物体原位置。 3. 绿(3) 物体不移动，直接擦除（置为背景色）。 4. 统计滑动后网格中红(2) 的总像素数（包括墙壁列的像素），记为 Pr；蓝(1) 的总像素数（包括墙壁列的像素），记为 Pb；绿(3) 的原始总像素数，记为 Pg。 5. 创建新的输出网格。分别构建三个实心正方形：红色正方形边长 sqrt(Pr)，蓝色正方形边长 sqrt(Pb)，绿色正方形边长 sqrt(Pg)。 6. 将三个正方形按面积从小到大从左到右排列，底边对齐，相邻正方形之间留一列背景色间隔。输出网格高度为最大正方形的边长，宽度为三个正方形宽度加两列间隔之和。  **关键洞察**：墙壁列的像素也计入颜色总数——滑动不仅改变物体位置，还通过"合并到墙壁"增大了红/蓝的有效像素数。观察者必须注意墙壁像素是否计入，这需要对比多个示例中墙壁列长度与输出正方形边长的关系才能确认。绿色物体虽不滑动也不出现在中间结果中，但其像素数仍参与最终排列。  --- </new_puzzle>  ## 机制相似参考题  下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：优先使用新题中已经写明的原语、组合逻辑、来源原语和显式参考题 id；再用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。  已选参考：eval/21897d95, train/f0100645, train/465b7d93, train/337b420f, train/df978a02, eval/a251c730, train/54dc2872, train/e9fc42f2  新题正文显式提及的参考题 id：1b8318e3, 20fb2937, 21897d95, 337b420f, 465b7d93, 50c07299, 54dc2872, 60d73be6, 758abdf0, 83eb0a57, 84ba50d3, 8abad3cf, 984d8a3e, 9caf5b84, a251c730, abc82100, df978a02, e9fc42f2, f0100645, f931b4a8  文件头参考题组 id（弱提示）：none  <reference_puzzle rank="1" source="eval" puzzle_id="21897d95"> <similarity> score=1.0925 mechanism=1.0000 lexical=0.0125 code_feature=0.7500 overlap_tags=none </similarity> <paths> code=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/21897d95.py annotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/21897d95.json </paths> <description> Repaint regions from T-shaped control markers, erase the markers, and optionally rotate based on a color-9 L-marker.  Input structure: - The grid is a mosaic of monochrome regions. - Color 1 forms T-shaped control markers on region boundaries. - Some controls use three singleton color-1 pixels around a colored center; that center is a literal replacement color. - An optional 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker triggers 90-degree rotation of the output.  Rule: - For a color-1 T marker, the single stem points at the destination region to repaint. - The two diagonal cells behind the stem identify the source region; the destination gets that source region's original color. - For a colored-center T marker, the same stem identifies the destination, but the center color is the replacement. - All marker cells are filled with the final color of the source-side region. - A 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker controls rotation: ┐ (corner top-right) → CCW 90°, ┌ (corner top-left) → CW 90°.  Key insight: - The stem chooses what changes, while the two diagonals behind the stem choose where the marker itself belongs. </description> <annotation> {   "type": "transform_in_place",   "src": "monochrome regions with T-shaped color-1 control markers",   "transform": "recolor the region pointed to by each T stem using the original color from the two diagonal source cells behind the stem; colored-center T markers use the center color instead; erase marker cells into the source-side region",   "grid_shape": "same, except rotate 90 degrees when indicated by the colored-center control orientation",   "notes": "small non-rectangular colored scraps are absorbed into the neighboring region" } </annotation> </reference_puzzle>  <reference_puzzle rank="2" source="train" puzzle_id="f0100645"> <similarity> score=1.0702 mechanism=1.0000 lexical=0.0083 code_feature=0.5714 overlap_tags=none </similarity> <paths> code=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/f0100645.py annotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/f0100645.json </paths> <description> Slide each inner colored object horizontally into the same-colored vertical wall until it touches an obstacle.  Input structure - The background is the dominant color. - The only foreground colors are two non-background colors. - One foreground color fills the left column and the other fills the right column. - Extra 8-connected objects of each wall color appear away from that color's wall.  Rule - Clear the extra objects from their original positions. - For each wall color, process its 8-connected extra objects from nearest to farthest from the matching wall. - Slide each object horizontally toward its matching wall as far as possible without overlapping the wall or an already settled object of the same color. - Keep the two vertical wall columns fixed.  Key insight - The side columns act like color-specific gravity walls: same-colored objects compact sideways against their own wall while preserving each object's shape. </description> <annotation> {   "type": "move_along_path",   "src": "8-connected objects away from the full-height side wall of the same color",   "path": "horizontal slide toward the matching side wall, stopping just before the wall or an already settled same-color object would overlap",   "trajectory": "translate each object rigidly to its final unobstructed position",   "transform": "clear original object positions, keep both side walls fixed, and preserve each moved object's color and shape",   "multi_step": "For each wall color, settle objects from nearest to farthest from that wall so later objects can stop against earlier same-color objects." } </annotation> </reference_puzzle>  <reference_puzzle rank="3" source="train" puzzle_id="465b7d93"> <similarity> score=1.0646 mechanism=1.0000 lexical=0.0228 code_feature=0.5000 overlap_tags=none </similarity> <paths> code=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/465b7d93.py annotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/465b7d93.json </paths> <description> Move the small colored sprite into the hollow frame by stretching its shape to the frame interior.  Input structure: - The background is the dominant color. - There are exactly two foreground colors: one forms a complete rectangular   one-pixel-thick frame, and the other forms one 4-connected sprite outside it. - The frame interior is initially background.  Rule: - Clear the original sprite from its outside location. - Map the sprite bbox to the frame interior bbox, sending bbox extremes to   interior extremes. - Draw straight horizontal or vertical segments between mapped positions of   adjacent sprite pixels, then fill any enclo